WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.060
Speaker 1: Donald Trump is now furious that
Ron DeSantis stole one of his lines.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.540
But the truth is that Trump stole the line
from Reagan.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.760
They're just stealing the same stuff from
each other back and forth.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:12.760
Okay.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.760
Talking Points Memo Article.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.370
Trump attacked DeSantis for blatantly plagiarizing
a speech line that Trump actually took from

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.370
Reagan.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.560
Trump actually took from Reagan.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.640
The line is the great American comeback.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:32.360
So team Trump published this video of Trump
using the line in 2020, and then DeSantis

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.960
using it now, meaning to prove that DeSantis
stole it from Trump.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.050
Speaker 2: Three years ago, we launched the
Great American Comeback.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.050
Right?

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.640
Tonight, I stand before you to share the incredible
results.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.809
I'm Ron DeSantis, and I'm running for president
to lead our great American comeback.

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:59.769
Speaker 1: So this is like the perfect microcosm
of what I expect the 2024 Republican primary

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:00.769
to be.

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:06.570
Trump attacked DeSantis for stealing the phrase
great American comeback.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.810
In reality, Trump took the term from Ronald
Reagan.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.520
Trump didn't invent it, by the way.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.700
He also didn't accomplish the great American
comeback.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.799
But that's a different thing.

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:20.460
If you do a Lexis Nexis search for that term,
you have hundreds of pages of results.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.460
Okay.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.979
The phrase great American comeback has been
used in speeches for so long.

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:32.810
But you go back to Reagan's State of the Union
speech in I believe it's 86, and there it

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:39.780
was that in that particular speech, Reagan
bragged about 37 straight months of economic

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.530
growth and falling interest rates.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.720
And he said it's because of conservative values.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.030
And he talked about the great American comeback.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.040
So Trump didn't invent it.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.860
If you want to argue that anybody has a claim
to these phrases, it would be Reagan.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:56.860
Also important.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.770
Trump didn't make up Make America Great Again.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:04.740
Reagan used a slightly different version of
it back in 1980 where he said, Let's make

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.110
America great again.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.470
Let's make America great again.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:13.800
So my view is these are not such unique phrases
that anybody really, really holds a right

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.800
or not.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.400
Obviously, it's not a legal right, but even
sort of like a moral right to them.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.739
These are very general phrases in many ways.

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:26.310
But to the extent that the idea is that these
are unique messages from Republican candidates,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.350
they're not.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:31.739
And Trump yelling at someone for stealing
something from him that he already stole from

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:35.129
someone else is pretty damn funny.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:41.269
I expect this to be exactly the type of issue
that these Republicans argue about during

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:42.670
the during this campaign.

